---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const updated = "26 August 2026";
---

<Layout
  title={"Privacy Policy — Al Marfa Apps"}
  description="Privacy policy for Al Marfa Technologies apps — no accounts or ads; Al Quran Android uses anonymous aggregate Search analytics with an opt-out."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 py-8 sm:py-10 min-w-0">
    <nav class="text-xs text-fg-3 mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-[#C9A84C]">Home</a> → Privacy Policy
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-fg-3 mb-8">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        This policy covers the mobile apps published by
        <strong class="text-fg">Al Marfa Technologies</strong> — currently
        <strong class="text-fg">Al Quran</strong> and
        <strong class="text-fg">Sharah Kitab at-Tawheed</strong> — and this
        website, <a href="https://kitabattawheed.com" class="text-[#C9A84C] hover:underline">kitabattawheed.com</a>.
        Our apps are built to be private by design: there are
        <strong class="text-fg">no accounts, no advertising, no third-party
        analytics or crash-reporting SDKs, and no advertising trackers</strong>.
        Al Quran uses a narrowly scoped first-party, anonymous Search analytics
        service on Android; Sharah Kitab at-Tawheed does not use app analytics.
      </p>
    </section>

    <aside class="mb-10 rounded-xl border border-[#C9A84C]/35 bg-[#C9A84C]/10 p-4 sm:p-5">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-fg mb-2">Al Quran now has a dedicated policy</h2>
      <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed">
        This shared page remains available for older app releases and keeps the
        current summary below. The canonical, app-specific version is
        <a
          href="https://alquranreader.com/privacy/"
          class="text-[#C9A84C] hover:underline font-semibold"
        >Al Quran's dedicated privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
    </aside>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#C9A84C] mb-3">The short version</h2>
      <ul class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-3 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
        <li>We do not collect your identity, searches, reading positions, location, bookmarks, or advertising identifiers.</li>
        <li>Everything an app remembers (your place in the text or audio, bookmarks, downloads, and settings) is stored <strong class="text-fg">only on your device</strong>.</li>
        <li>Your <strong class="text-fg">location never leaves your device</strong> — it is used only by Al Quran to calculate prayer times locally.</li>
        <li>Al Quran for Android sends anonymous Search interaction and coarse performance counts by default. You can disable this in Settings.</li>
        <li>Other network activity is content you ask for: streaming or downloading audio, and fetching an app's catalogue. No identifiers or accounts are sent.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#C9A84C] mb-3">What the apps store on your device</h2>
      <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        To make reading and listening comfortable, the apps keep small files
        locally: your last position, bookmarks, downloaded audio, and your
        preferences (language, theme, font size, and similar). In
        <strong class="text-fg">Al Quran</strong> this also includes your
        reminder and reading-light settings; in
        <strong class="text-fg">Sharah Kitab at-Tawheed</strong> it includes your
        lecture progress, downloaded lectures, and study progress. This data
        stays in the app's private storage and is removed when you uninstall the
        app. Al Quran's anonymous analytics queue is described separately below.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#C9A84C] mb-3">Anonymous Search analytics (Al Quran for Android only)</h2>
      <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        Al Quran records a closed set of anonymous events so we can tell whether
        Search is fast and useful: opening Search, submitting and completing a
        search, opening a result, the Detailed reader becoming ready, and leaving
        that reader handoff. It sends only coarse buckets such as query length,
        result count, latency, rank, source kind, dwell time, and app/build
        version. It never sends search text or hashes, Qur'an positions,
        translation or reciter names, bookmarks, reading history, location,
        account data, advertising IDs, or a stable device, installation, or
        session identifier.
      </p>
      <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        Events wait in a small bounded on-device queue and upload over HTTPS when
        the app is idle or backgrounded, normally no more than once per day.
        Cloudflare processes these requests for us. Like any internet service,
        Cloudflare receives transient network metadata such as an IP address to
        deliver the request; our analytics service does not copy it into the
        analytics dataset or log the request body.
      </p>
      <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        To prevent a lost network response from counting the same upload twice,
        each upload carries a new random batch code. The same code is reused only
        when retrying that exact upload; it is never reused as a device,
        installation, account, or session identifier. Cloudflare D1 keeps this
        code only for retry deduplication. It expires after eight days, and daily
        cleanup removes it within the following day. Apart from this short-lived
        operational receipt, we retain only aggregate daily counters. Neither can
        be traced back to a person or device.
      </p>
      <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        Disable this at any time under <strong class="text-fg">Settings → Help
        improve Search</strong>. Doing so stops future collection and deletes
        queued events. Sharah Kitab at-Tawheed and the iOS build of Al Quran do
        not currently send app analytics.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#C9A84C] mb-3">When the apps use the internet</h2>
      <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        Both apps work offline. Apart from Al Quran's anonymous Android analytics
        described above, when you actively request online content the app makes a
        standard web request to fetch it. Nothing is uploaded with these content
        requests:
      </p>
      <ul class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-3 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
        <li><strong class="text-fg">Al Quran</strong> — optional recitation and downloadable content are fetched from Al Quran's Cloudflare-hosted content network and supported source providers, then cached where appropriate for offline use.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-fg">Sharah Kitab at-Tawheed</strong> — the lecture catalogue and lecture audio are fetched from our own content network on <a href="https://kitabattawheed.com" class="text-[#C9A84C] hover:underline">kitabattawheed.com</a> (Cloudflare) when you browse, stream, or download a lecture.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        As with any web request, the server providing that content sees the
        request's IP address and which file was asked for — this is inherent to
        how the internet works. The apps send no user identifiers, accounts, or
        advertising identifiers along with content requests.
        Cloudflare's practices are described in its
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-[#C9A84C] hover:underline">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#C9A84C] mb-3">Location (Al Quran only)</h2>
      <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        If you use prayer times in <strong class="text-fg">Al Quran</strong>, the
        app asks for your device's location. Prayer times are calculated
        <strong class="text-fg">entirely on your device</strong>; your location is
        not sent to any server. If you decline the permission, the rest of the app
        works normally. Sharah Kitab at-Tawheed does not request location at all.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#C9A84C] mb-3">Notifications</h2>
      <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        All notifications are <strong class="text-fg">local</strong> — scheduled
        and shown by your device, never pushed from a server. Al Quran uses them
        for Sunnah and prayer-time reminders (and on Android may request the
        exact-alarm capability so reminders fire on time); Sharah Kitab at-Tawheed
        uses them for download progress and audio playback controls. No
        notification data leaves your device, and neither app uses push
        notifications.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#C9A84C] mb-3">What we don't do</h2>
      <ul class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-3 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
        <li>No third-party analytics or crash-reporting SDKs in the apps.</li>
        <li>No search text, Qur'an positions, reading history, or stable identifiers in Al Quran's first-party analytics.</li>
        <li>No advertising and no advertising identifiers.</li>
        <li>No accounts, sign-ins, or cloud sync.</li>
        <li>No selling or sharing analytics data and no advertising profiles.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#C9A84C] mb-3">This website</h2>
      <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        This site (kitabattawheed.com) uses
        <strong class="text-fg">Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong>, which is
        cookieless and measures only aggregate, anonymous traffic (such as page
        views and referrers) — it builds no cross-site profile of you and sets no
        tracking cookies. On-site search runs entirely in your browser. The site
        shows no ads.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#C9A84C] mb-3">Children</h2>
      <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        Both apps are suitable for all ages and are listed for a general 13+
        audience. Al Quran's anonymous Android analytics does not collect names,
        contact details, identifiers, precise location, searches, or reading
        history from any reader, including children who may use the app.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#C9A84C] mb-3">Deleting your data</h2>
      <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        Uninstalling removes local preferences, downloads, and queued analytics
        events. Al Quran's analytics switch deletes its queue without requiring
        an uninstall. Server-side analytics consists of anonymous aggregate
        counters plus the short-lived random deduplication receipt described
        above, so there is no account, device record, or personal profile to
        locate or delete.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#C9A84C] mb-3">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        If a future version of an app changes any of the above (for example, a new
        online feature), we will update this policy and revise the date above
        before that version ships.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#C9A84C] mb-3">Contact</h2>
      <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed">
        Questions about privacy? Email
        <a href="mailto:hello@almarfa.co" class="text-[#C9A84C] hover:underline">hello@almarfa.co</a>
        — <strong class="text-fg">Al Marfa Technologies</strong>,
        <a href="https://almarfa.co" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-[#C9A84C] hover:underline">almarfa.co</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
